---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **들어온 자리가 얼마나 갈지를 말해 주나.** (`/opening`)
 *
 * ── 왜 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   첫 주 월요일에 있는 사실은 하나다 — 어느 자리에 떴나. 그것뿐이다.
 *   /exit(나갈 때)와 /run-length(얼마나)는 쟀는데 **그 둘을 이은 적이 없었다.**
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **예보로 읽히지 않게 한다.** 이 표는 수천 구간의 평균이고 자리마다 흩어짐이 넓다.
 *    그 말을 작게 쓰지 않는다 — 화면에 크게 적는다.
 * ⛔ **영화와 시리즈를 안 섞는다.** 한국 영화는 남과 같고 시리즈만 다르다.
 * ⛔ **한국 아닌 것도 같이 낸다.** 「높이 들어오면 오래 간다」는 어디서나 참일 수 있다.
 * ⛔ 자리를 「좋은 것/나쁜 것」으로 안 쓴다. **들어온 칸**이다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 * ⚠ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `wikitip-opening.json` 에서 읽는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-opening.json';

const 찾 = (g) => d.byGroup.find((x) => x.group === g);
const 한시 = 찾('한국 시리즈');
const 영어이름 = {
  '한국 시리즈': 'Korean series',
  '그 밖 시리즈': 'Every other series',
  '한국 영화': 'Korean films',
  '그 밖 영화': 'Every other film',
};
const 차례 = ['한국 시리즈', '그 밖 시리즈', '한국 영화', '그 밖 영화'].map(찾);
const 총잘림 = d.byGroup.reduce((s, g) => s + g.truncated, 0);

const TITLE = 'What an opening position buys — Korean titles on Netflix country charts';
const DESC =
  `A Korean series that opens at number one runs a median of ${한시.topEntryMedian} weeks; one that `
  + `opens at ten runs ${한시.bottomEntryMedian}. Across ${한시.runs.toLocaleString('en-US')} runs that is `
  + `${d.koreanSeriesSlope} weeks a position, against ${d.otherSeriesSlope} for other series and `
  + `${d.otherFilmSlope} for other films.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10', 'https://www.wikidata.org'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/opening">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Korean series opening at 1 — median <b>{한시.topEntryMedian}</b> weeks.
    Opening at 10 — <b>{한시.bottomEntryMedian}</b>.
  </p>

  <section class="warn-box">
    <h2>Before the table: this is not a forecast</h2>
    <p class="warn">
      Everything below is an average over thousands of runs, and <b>the spread inside every position
      is wide</b>. Of the runs that opened at position 8, {한시.byEntry[7].fourPlusPc}% still reached
      four weeks; of those that opened at number one, {(100 - 한시.byEntry[0].fourPlusPc).toFixed(1)}%
      did not. A single title can sit anywhere in that spread.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Korean series, by the position they opened at</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Opened at</th><th>Runs</th><th>Median weeks</th>
            <th>Lasting 4+ weeks</th><th>Gone after one week</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {한시.byEntry.map((e) => (
            <tr class={e.entry === 1 || e.entry === 10 ? 'edge' : undefined}>
              <td class="nm">{e.entry}</td>
              <td>{e.runs.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td class="tot">{e.medianWeeks}</td>
              <td>{e.fourPlusPc}%</td>
              <td>{e.oneWeekPc}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><b>{d.unit}</b></p>
    <p class="note">
      The middle of the table is where it turns. Above position five most runs reach four weeks;
      below it most do not.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The same measurement for everyone else</h2>
    <p class="body">{d.whyBothFormats}</p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th></th><th>Runs</th><th>Median weeks opening at 1</th>
            <th>Opening at 10</th><th>Weeks per position</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {차례.map((g) => (
            <tr class={g.group.startsWith('한국') ? 'edge' : undefined}>
              <td class="nm">{영어이름[g.group]}</td>
              <td>{g.runs.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td>{g.topEntryMedian}</td>
              <td>{g.bottomEntryMedian}</td>
              <td class="tot">{g.weeksPerStep}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">{d.whySlopeNotRegression}</p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>Position is worth more in series than in films</b> — {d.koreanSeriesSlope} and{' '}
      {d.otherSeriesSlope} against {d.koreanFilmSlope} and {d.otherFilmSlope}. A film's run is short
      whatever it opens at, so there is less room for the opening to matter.
    </p>
    <p class="q">
      And it is worth more for Korean titles in both formats: <b>{d.koreanSeriesSlope}</b> against{' '}
      {d.otherSeriesSlope} in series, <b>{d.koreanFilmSlope}</b> against {d.otherFilmSlope} in films.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      That is a different statement from "Korean titles last longer", which is{' '}
      <a href="/run-length">true of series only</a>. This one says the first week <em>tells you
      more</em> — the distance between a good opening and a bad one is wider.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>How this was counted, and what it cannot say</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Source</b> — {d.source}</li>
      <li><b>Rows read</b> — {d.rowsRead.toLocaleString('en-US')}; {d.rowsOverwritten} rows could not be
        resolved to a single run and are reported rather than hidden.</li>
      <li><b>Unfinished runs</b> — {d.whyTruncatedRemoved} That is {총잘림.toLocaleString('en-US')} runs.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="warn">{d.cannotAnswer}</p>
    <p class="note">
      It also cannot tell you <b>why</b>. A title that opens at number one had something behind it —
      a marketing push, a returning cast, a second season — and none of that is in a rank table. The
      opening position is a symptom of whatever produced it, not a cause of what follows.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/run-length">How long a title holds a chart</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/exit">How a title leaves</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/climb">Is the week it enters its highest</a> · <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/opening" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .warn-box { border-left: 3px solid #b45309; padding-left: 1rem; }
</style>
